227
00:13:31,822 --> 00:13:40,849
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course that Wilson, you know, he drove in 190 runs and I don't think that record will ever be broken.

228
00:13:40,909 --> 00:13:43,371
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't care how much rabbit they put in the ball at all.

229
00:13:43,611 --> 00:13:44,732
[SPEAKER_02]: That was 1930.

230
00:13:44,752 --> 00:13:46,634
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, he was very fortunate then.

231
00:13:47,803 --> 00:13:54,846
[SPEAKER_01]: because he had those guys like Hartnett and Kyler and Stevenson getting on base every time they went to bat.

232
00:13:55,127 --> 00:13:57,408
