272
00:16:42,778 --> 00:16:44,199
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, well, I...

273
00:16:45,804 --> 00:16:47,645
[SPEAKER_01]: All right, I didn't like to.

274
00:16:48,385 --> 00:16:50,486
[SPEAKER_01]: I played regular on the Pittsburgh ball club.

275
00:16:51,606 --> 00:16:53,827
[SPEAKER_01]: But I like Chicago.

276
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:55,608
[SPEAKER_01]: Paul Parson.

277
00:16:56,028 --> 00:16:57,049
[SPEAKER_02]: I noticed here.

278
00:16:57,229 --> 00:17:01,651
[SPEAKER_01]: The last place ball club, and I figured that I'd have a pretty good chance.

279
00:17:01,711 --> 00:17:01,951
[SPEAKER_01]: Hi.

280
00:17:02,331 --> 00:17:02,771
[SPEAKER_02]: How you doing?

281
00:17:03,011 --> 00:17:04,072
[SPEAKER_02]: Very good, thanks.

282
00:17:04,432 --> 00:17:09,334
[SPEAKER_02]: I noticed here that your home run output dropped off somewhat when you went over to Chicago.

283
00:17:09,394 --> 00:17:10,934
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, yeah.

284
00:17:11,035 --> 00:17:14,436
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I went over there, and they start pitching out away from me, and I just

285
00:17:14,930 --> 00:17:21,352
[SPEAKER_01]: hit the ball where it was pitched, my power was left center.

286
00:17:22,012 --> 00:17:27,994
[SPEAKER_02]: And I was a pull hitter in Pittsburgh.

287
00:17:28,394 --> 00:17:30,634
[SPEAKER_01]: Pittsburgh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

288
00:17:30,694 --> 00:17:34,916
[SPEAKER_01]: And they had a low fence there, chicken wire in front of it.

289
00:17:38,196 --> 00:17:41,157
[SPEAKER_01]: But I wasn't ever a home run hitter, power hitter.

290
00:17:44,505 --> 00:17:54,313
[SPEAKER_01]: I hit the ball where they pitched, get a ball inside, pull it to right field, and out away from me.

291
00:17:55,234 --> 00:17:56,795
[SPEAKER_01]: I had power in the left center.

292
00:17:58,757 --> 00:18:00,638
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you have any pitchers you didn't like to bat against?

293
00:18:00,818 --> 00:18:01,859
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, Dutch Ruther.

294
00:18:03,581 --> 00:18:05,382
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't have much trouble with any lefty.

295
00:18:05,422 --> 00:18:10,806
[SPEAKER_01]: I played every day, but Dutch Ruther was a menace to me.

296
00:18:10,826 --> 00:18:12,488
[SPEAKER_01]: I hit a little foul off of him one day,

297
00:18:13,338 --> 00:18:19,860
[SPEAKER_01]: called time, come in and walked in, and Bill Clem was the umpire, and he said, well Dutch, what do you want?

298
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:22,500
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, I don't want to talk to you, Bill.

299
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:24,001
