00:19:49,341 --> 00:19:52,583
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, they call them brushback pitches.

330
00:19:53,343 --> 00:19:54,383
[SPEAKER_01]: They tipped you over.

331
00:19:54,483 --> 00:19:57,464
[SPEAKER_02]: Is there any spitballers still pitching when you were?

332
00:19:57,604 --> 00:19:58,905
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, oh yeah.

333
00:19:59,225 --> 00:20:00,786
[SPEAKER_01]: Willie Grimes, Phil Douglas.

334
00:20:01,686 --> 00:20:04,387
[SPEAKER_01]: They throw a few now, too, don't think they don't.

335
00:20:05,367 --> 00:20:06,328
[SPEAKER_02]: They're legal then now.

336
00:20:06,348 --> 00:20:06,588
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

337
00:20:09,670 --> 00:20:11,631
[SPEAKER_02]: What about Hornby as a manager?

338
00:20:13,453 --> 00:20:16,535
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, a lot of ballplayers didn't get along with him.

339
00:20:16,595 --> 00:20:17,416
[SPEAKER_01]: I got along with him.

340
00:20:18,376 --> 00:20:25,202
[SPEAKER_01]: As long as you were delivering and hustling for him, it didn't make any difference how good you were going or how bad you were going.

341
00:20:26,102 --> 00:20:27,103
[SPEAKER_01]: He wouldn't say anything to you.

342
00:20:27,123 --> 00:20:28,144
[SPEAKER_01]: He was strictly a loner.

343
00:20:28,884 --> 00:20:31,586
[SPEAKER_01]: Never patted anybody on the back, you know what I mean?

344
00:20:32,087 --> 00:20:36,270
[SPEAKER_01]: He expected every ballplayer, he was very much like Ty Cobb.

345
00:20:36,995 --> 00:20:40,917
[SPEAKER_01]: Ty Cobb expected every ball player that played for him to be as good as he was.

346
00:20:41,537 --> 00:20:50,641
[SPEAKER_01]: Hornby was very much, as far as hitting was concerned, he expected everybody in his lineup to hit as good as he hit, and that was an impossibility.

347
00:20:51,402 --> 00:20:52,342
[SPEAKER_01]: Nobody could do that.

348
00:20:52,662 --> 00:20:56,344
[SPEAKER_01]: Because he was a great right-hand hitter.

349
00:20:56,604 --> 00:20:58,525
[SPEAKER_01]: But he stayed completely away.

350
00:20:58,565 --> 00:21:03,267
[SPEAKER_01]: There was no discussions or anything.

351
00:21:04,392 --> 00:21:07,314
[SPEAKER_01]: in the clubhouse with any of his ballplayers.

352
00:21:07,334 --> 00:21:11,777
[SPEAKER_01]: He'd come in, take his uniform off, go to the hotel, and that was it.

353
00:21:11,797 --> 00:21:13,338
[SPEAKER_01]: See him the next day at the ballpark.

354
00:21:15,059 --> 00:21:18,341
[SPEAKER_02]: They say if he saw anybody with newspaper in there, he'd take it away from them.

355
00:21:18,501 --> 00:21:19,162
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's right.

356
00:21:19,182 --> 00:21:22,544
[SPEAKER_01]: He didn't allow any smoking in the clubhouse, the newspaper.

357
00:21:24,005 --> 00:21:25,926
[SPEAKER_02]: Must have been a real change when you took over.

358
00:21:26,006 --> 00:21:27,227
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, it was.

359
00:21:27,507 --> 00:21:27,987
[SPEAKER_02]: It was.

360
00:21:28,047 --> 00:21:28,828
[SPEAKER_01]: I turned them loose.

361
00:21:29,208 --> 00:21:30,209
[SPEAKER_02]: One of the team wasn't the best.

362
00:21:30,229 --> 00:21:30,549
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

363
00:21:33,301 --> 00:21:34,702
[SPEAKER_01]: I got along fine with Rog.

364
00:21:37,844 --> 00:21:39,325
[SPEAKER_02]: He loved the ponies, didn't he?

365
00:21:39,345 --> 00:21:41,306
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, to a great extent.

366
00:21:41,346 --> 00:21:47,551
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know how much, whether he won on them or what, but... Well, the 32 World Series.

367
00:21:48,071 --> 00:21:51,353
[SPEAKER_02]: Was that four straight?

368
00:21:52,174 --> 00:21:52,814
[SPEAKER_01]: Four straight.

369
00:21:53,494 --> 00:21:54,395
[SPEAKER_01]: Never come close.

370
00:21:56,096 --> 00:21:58,097
[SPEAKER_02]: What about that called shot by the Bay?

371
00:21:58,578 --> 00:22:00,819
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's the only one guy that was under the gun.

372
00:22:00,879 --> 00:22:01,780
[SPEAKER_01]: Harden said he didn't

